# Normalise line endings in the repository, and check them out as LF on every
# platform, Windows included.
#
# Why this is not optional here: with only core.autocrlf=true and no
# .gitattributes, a Windows clone checks out CRLF, and Astro's build silently
# drops ALL CSS on such a checkout. The culprit is the CSS emitted for the
# katex.min.css import in src/layouts/LayoutMath.astro - Vite inlines a
# JavaScript parser for it, the CRLF breaks it, and the build completes with
# exit code 0 and unstyled pages. The only symptom is pages with no <style> and
# no .css assets, which is easy to miss because nothing errors.
#
# eol=lf is safe for every platform: macOS and Linux already use LF, so their
# working trees are unaffected. Editors that prefer CRLF are overridden at
# checkout, which is the point.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
